  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule (hydrocodone skeleton) is present in the supplied records; the decision relies on structurally related morphinan/opioid comparators and the physicochemical prior.",
    "Most high opioid F values are from cirrhotic patients; pentazocine's healthy control F was 0.18 (C68), so disease-state values can overestimate healthy-state F, but morphine (~47% healthy), pethidine (0.48 normal), and samidorphan (69% healthy) support F>=20% without cirrhosis.",
    "The only subthreshold F record (S-raclopride in rats, 17%, C53) is not transferable due to species and structural dissimilarity.",
    "No formulation-, dose-, or prandial-state-specific data for the query are supplied."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction high: the query is a 3-methoxy-N-methyl-morphinan-6-one (hydrocodone skeleton) with favorable physicochemical properties, and all transferable opioid/morphinan records show absolute oral bioavailability at or above 20% (morphine 27.7-154%, pethidine 0.48-0.87, pentazocine 0.68-0.70 in cirrhosis, samidorphan 69%). New L2 records reinforce this; the only subthreshold F record is non-transferable. Confidence high because the evidence is consistent and the threshold is modest, though no direct query-specific F is available."
}

